WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.180
Petyr Baelish, known as Littlefinger, is one
of the most intriguing characters in Game

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:09.570
of Thrones. He's quietly powerful, a clever
manipulator, sharp-tongued and more than slightly

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:14.049
creepy. Littlefinger has said that he tries
to keep his foes confused by his actions,

00:00:14.049 --> 00:00:19.040
and watching Game of Thrones, you may be pretty
confused yourself. Petyr has betrayed Ned,

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.450
snogged Sansa, killed Lysa, and been competing
with Varys in a dramatic stare competition

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:29.160
for four seasons now. What's he trying to
achieve? Who is this guy?

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.449
Unlike most of the major players of the Game
of Thrones, Littlefinger comes from a small

00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:37.179
and unimportant noble family which holds a
piece of land here, at the Fingers – one of

00:00:37.179 --> 00:00:41.839
the little ones. Because of his father's friendship
with Hoster Tully, Petyr was lucky enough

00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:48.070
to be raised at Riverrun, growing up with
Edmure, Lysa and Catelyn. Lysa loved Littlefinger,

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:52.289
but Littlefinger only had eyes for Cat. When
Catelyn was to be married to Brandon Stark,

00:00:52.289 --> 00:00:56.710
young Petyr went so far as to challenge Brandon
to a spectacularly unsucessful duel which

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:01.519
left him scarred in more ways than one. In
any case, Brandon got himself killed by the

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:05.640
Mad King, Catelyn ended up with his brother
Ned, and Littlefinger never won the love of

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.830
his dear Cat.
These events shaped Petyr as a man. "You know

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:16.830
what I learnt losing that duel? I learnt that
I'll never win. Not that way. That's their

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:24.400
game, their rules. I'm not going to fight
them – I'm going to fuck them".

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:30.630
He learned that to get what he wants he has to
be indirect and strategic using tools more

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:35.350
subtle that the sword. So it was his political
and financial brilliance – and his friends

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:39.390
in high places – that drove his rapid rise
up the ranks to the position of Master of

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:43.250
Coin – basically the treasurer – for King
Robert, who managed to spend the Throne into

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:48.230
debt despire the huge amount of money Petyr
was bringing in. Petyr used his power carefully,

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:52.640
buying up property and businesses, like brothels,
establishing a network of spies, and placing

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:57.670
men loyal to him in useful places.
And then Season 1 begins, with the death of

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:02.350
the Hand of the King, Jon Arryn.
We find out in Season 4 that the killer of

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:08.000
Jon Arryn was his wife, Lysa. Littlefinger
got Lysa, his childhood friend and the woman

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.299
who's still devoted to him, to poison Jon
and then tell her sister Catelyn that the

00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:15.579
Lannisters did it.
When Catelyn comes to King's Landing to tell

00:02:15.579 --> 00:02:19.840
Ned about the attempted killing of Bran (which
was possibly ordered by Joffrey but we don't

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.219
know), Littlefinger lies and tells Catelyn
that the dagger used was Tyrion's, leading

00:02:24.219 --> 00:02:29.249
Cat to capture and wrongly accuse the dwarf.
Meanwhile, Petyr helps Ned uncover Jamie and

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:33.749
Cersei's incestuous secret, but when Eddard
confronts the Lannisters, Petyr betrays him,

00:02:33.749 --> 00:02:38.189
and soon Ned's dead.
All three of these moves were deliberate attempts

00:02:38.189 --> 00:02:43.659
by Littlefinger to create conflict between
the Lannisters and the Starks. And it works.

00:02:43.659 --> 00:02:50.019
Petyr Baelish – indirectly, without implicating himself – started the War of the Five Kings.

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:56.060
But why? Petyr says that "chaos is a ladder". Littlefinger

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:01.700
is using the chaos of war to gain power. For example, in Season 2, Littlefinger negotiates

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.349
an alliance with the Tyrells. This alliance
saves the Lannisters in the Battle of Blackwater,

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:11.450
so Littlefinger is rewarded with the castle
of Harrenhal, and rule of the Riverlands.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:15.340
With this higher status, and again because
of the war, Littlefinger is sent to marry

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:19.529
Lysa, in order to secure the military support
of the Vale, just about the only region untouched

00:03:19.529 --> 00:03:25.480
by the war. So he goes and marries the woman
who loves him. And then he kills her. With

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:30.769
Lysa gone, and Jon Arryn already dead, Robert
Arryn is the only thing standing between Littlefinger

00:03:30.769 --> 00:03:37.769
and control of the Vale. Wouldn't be terrible
if sick, frail Sweetrobin somehow had an accident?

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:44.999
On his way out of King's Landing, Petyr does
two things – he helps kill King Joffrey, and

00:03:44.999 --> 00:03:49.060
he takes Sansa Stark. He helped kill Joffrey
presumably to create more of the chaos that

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:52.859
he's been doing so well out of but possibly
also to gain favour with the Tyrells, now

00:03:52.859 --> 00:03:58.159
one of the most powerful houses. But why did
he take Sansa? It's obvious that he's attracted

00:03:58.159 --> 00:04:01.680
to her, and whether you want to call that
love or some kind of creepy-ass paedo shit

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:06.279
it seems to be related to Littlefinger's love
of Cat. He's projecting his love of the dead

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:09.930
mother onto the daughter – yeah it's really more this
isn't it.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:14.510
So that's one reason Petyr takes Sansa. But
there's another – as the last known living

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:19.280
Stark, Sansa is the "key to the North". Whoever
marries her becomes the Lord of Winterfell,

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.750
and has some claim on the North. Of course,
Sansa is already married, so her current husband

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:28.020
Tyrion would have to die for her to marry
again, but how could the brother of the Queen

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:34.090
possibly die? Ah. Littlefinger, by the way,
was the one to arrange this little entertainment,

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:37.900
which succeeded in creating public conflict
between Tyrion and Joffrey just before the

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.090
King died, helping to frame Tyrion for the
murder and be sentenced to death, freeing

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:46.860
Sansa up for marriage – or, it would've if
Tyrion didn't escape.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:52.210
Anyway. So at the start of Season 1, Petyr
Baelish was Master of Coin at King's Landing,

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:56.710
with this little nowhere as his official seat.
Now, he's sitting in the Eyrie, probably the

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:01.270
safest place in Westeros, with control of
the Vale, of the Riverlands, potentially of

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:05.389
the North, and with the embodiment of dead
woman he loves in an obsessive Gatsby-esque

00:05:05.389 --> 00:05:11.690
kind of a way. Without lifting a sword, he
has won the two things he desires – power

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:17.389
and Catelyn. Of course, both of those things
come with fairly large asterisks. He has Catelyn

00:05:17.389 --> 00:05:23.539
only in the form of her daughter, and his
control of these regions is doubtful. I mean,

00:05:23.539 --> 00:05:27.830
he has no army, no sworn lords backing him,
no love from the smallfolk, and a ruin for

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:32.080
a castle. But he does have the crown backing
his claim, at least on the Riverlands, so that's

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:37.099
gotta count for something. In any case he's
a long way from where he was before and he

00:05:37.099 --> 00:05:43.300
did it by creating and exploiting the chaos
of the War of the Five Kings. The question

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:49.120
now is – what next? It's hard to say. We've
never had a Littlefinger point of view chapter

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:56.120
and we only really see his actions indirectly.
Maybe he'll settle down. Or maybe on a ladder

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:02.460
the only way to go is up.
Thanks for watching this video. If there's

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:07.409
interest, similar videos on other characters
could follow. Who do you want to see explained?

